# Secure Linux (movereset): NEVER moved aside by "Reset this computer, keep my files" and NEVER packed by
# "Move my setup". One path per line, relative to the home folder; a folder line covers everything inside it.
# The tests check that no line of reset-settings.list or move-settings.list is, holds, or lies inside one of these.
#
# Your own folders of files
Desktop
Documents
Downloads
Music
Pictures
Videos
Templates
Public
# Keys, passwords and password safes
.ssh
.gnupg
.pki
.password-store
.local/share/keyrings
.local/share/kwalletd
.config/kwalletrc
.config/Bitwarden
.config/keepassxc
.cache/keepassxc
.local/share/keepassxc
.netrc
.git-credentials
.config/gh
.gitconfig
.config/git
.docker
.kube
.aws
.azure
# Secure Linux's own per-person records: backup settings and the backup key, app list, requests
.config/secure-linux
.local/state/secure-linux
.local/share/secure-linux
.config/borg
.cache/borg
# Browsers (bookmarks, saved passwords, history), messages, email
.mozilla
.librewolf
.config/BraveSoftware
.config/chromium
.config/google-chrome
.config/microsoft-edge
.thunderbird
.config/Signal
.config/Element
.config/evolution
.local/share/evolution
# App store apps and their data (each app keeps its own settings and sign-ins here)
.var
.local/share/flatpak
# Sync pairings, cloud and VPN sign-ins, authenticator codes
.config/syncthing
.local/state/syncthing
.config/rclone
.config/kdeconnect
.config/Nextcloud
.local/share/Nextcloud
.config/onedrive
.config/protonvpn
.config/Proton
.config/Mullvad VPN
.config/ente
.local/share/io.ente.auth
# Notes and documents kept by apps
.config/obsidian
.config/joplin-desktop
.local/share/Trash
